# SwiftPM build products. These are large, machine-specific, and regenerated
# by `swift build` — the same disposition as the Rust `target/` directory and
# the shell's `node_modules/`. Without this, a local `swift build` leaves
# several hundred MB of object files staged for commit.
.build/
*.o
*.swiftmodule
*.swiftdoc
*.swiftsourceinfo

# Package.resolved is NOT here on purpose (the 1.29.45 release's finding,
# 2026-11-15): it is SwiftPM's Cargo.lock — the dependency pins the tree was
# VERIFIED with. Untracked, every runner resolved the graph fresh from the
# floating `from:` ranges, and an upstream release landing between two runs
# changed the Cmlx resource-bundle emission under a green lane (the
# shell-macos assertion red 13:13Z→15:07Z with identical toolchains, the
# only mover being the fresh resolve). The pins file is COMMITTED and moves
# only as a named act (a dependency bump re-verifies first), the same
# discipline the Cargo.lock files and pnpm-lock.yaml already carry.

# The macOS lane's own log, if a local reproduction writes one.
shell-macos-ci.log
